This code uses the pigpio library to interact with the GPIO pins and the SPI interface. It sets up the SPI interface with the MCP3008 ADC, reads the analog output, and logs the timestamp and voltage to a file. The code also handles errors and retries failed SPI transfers. The alarm is turned off when the voltage is below 2.5V and turned on when the voltage exceeds 2.5V. The code also handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals by closing the log file, turning off the alarm, and invoking the pigpio cleanup function.

