This code uses the `spidev` library to interact with the SPI bus on the Raspberry Pi. It configures the SPI device to use a single-ended conversion on channel 0 with a 1 MHz clock and 3-byte SPI transfers. The program reads the raw ADC data from the DFRobot Soil Moisture Sensor v2.0, calculates the moisture percentage, and logs the data to the console every 5 seconds. The program also handles errors and releases the SPI file descriptor cleanly on program termination.

