This code uses the pigpio library to interact with the GPIO pins and the SPI bus. It initializes the SPI bus and the GPIO pins, reads the moisture level from the sensor, and activates the pump if the level is below the threshold. The pump is turned off after the specified duration. The program also logs the moisture level and pump activation/deactivation to a file named `irrigation.log`. The program can be configured with command-line options to set the threshold, pump duration, and sleep interval. If the program receives a SIGINT or SIGTERM signal, it turns off the pump and exits cleanly.

