Note: This code assumes that the Adafruit MAX9814 Electret Microphone Amplifier is connected to the MCP3008 10-bit ADC over the SPI bus with the following connections:

*   CS (Chip Select) to GPIO8
*   MOSI (Master Out Slave In) to GPIO10
*   MISO (Master In Slave Out) to GPIO9
*   SCLK (Clock) to GPIO11

Also, make sure to install the pigpio library and compile the code with the following command:

```bash
gcc -o sound_level_monitor sound_level_monitor.c -lpigpio
```

This code will continuously monitor the sound level and turn on the LED whenever the level exceeds the threshold. The LED will be turned off after a 10ms debounce period. The ambient noise level is calibrated during the first 5 seconds after startup.

