This code uses the `pigpio` library to interact with the GPIO hardware on the Raspberry Pi. It initializes the GPIO driver, sets up signal handlers for SIGINT, and sets up the servos. The main loop reads input from stdin, updates the servo positions based on the input, and delays between commands. The servos are cleaned up when the program exits.

