This code initializes the GPIO, sets up the I2C bus, opens the I2C handle, sets the I2C address, opens the log file, and enters a loop where it reads the distance from the sensor, converts it to meters, writes it to the log file, and sleeps for 100ms before repeating. If an I2C read fails, it logs a row with distance -1 and continues. The program also handles SIGINT to perform a graceful shutdown by closing the I2C handle, log file, and terminating the GPIO interface.

