This code uses the `pigpio` library to interact with the GPIO pins on the Raspberry Pi Zero W. It initializes the GPIO pins, sets up a signal handler for SIGINT, and measures the distance using the HC-SR04 ultrasonic sensor. The distance is calculated based on the pulse width of the echo signal and is logged to a file every second. If the distance is outside the valid range, an error message is printed and the program continues. The program releases all resources and exits cleanly on exit.

