This code uses the pigpio library to interact with the GPIO pins and the i2c library to communicate with the sensor. It sets up a signal handler to catch SIGINT and SIGTERM signals, which will clean up the GPIO and I2C resources when received. The code also uses the `i2c_rdwr` function to read the differential pressure from the sensor, computes the flow rate, logs the measurement to a file, and updates the PWM duty cycle to control the fan speed. The code handles errors and uses `perror` to print error messages to stderr.

