This code implements a flame detection system using the Keyes KY-026 Flame Sensor and an active buzzer connected to the GPIO bus. It polls the sensor every 500ms, detects a HIGH-to-LOW transition, logs a timestamped "FLAME DETECTED" entry to a file named "alert_log.txt", and drives the buzzer HIGH for 2 seconds. The system also logs a "System started" entry at startup and a "System stopped" entry on clean shutdown. The code handles every driver library call, file operation, and system call for failure, and exits cleanly with code 0 on any initialization error.

