This code uses the `pigpio` library to interact with the GPIO pins on the Raspberry Pi. It sets up the GPIO pin as an input with an internal pull-up, sets the pin as an interrupt for falling edges, and polls the pin every 100ms to detect a falling edge. When a falling edge is detected, it writes a timestamped message to the log file. The code also handles errors and ensures that the GPIO line is released and the log file is closed when the program exits. The `sigint_handler` function is installed to perform a clean shutdown when the program receives a SIGINT or SIGTERM signal.

