This code uses the `pigpio` library to interact with the GPIO pins and the `i2c` library to communicate with the LSM303DLHC magnetometer. It sets up signal handlers for SIGINT and SIGTERM to cleanly close the GPIO and I2C file descriptors when the program receives these signals. The program reads from the I2C bus every 100ms, extracts the Z-axis magnitude from the sensor data, and updates the brightness of an LED connected to GPIO17 based on the Z-axis magnitude. If an I2C error occurs, the program logs the error and skips the current sample without crashing.

