This code implements a self-balancing robot using PID-controlled motors and obstacle-avoidance from a simulated ultrasonic sensor. The robot uses the libgpiod library to control the motors and the pigpio library to initialize the GPIO pins. The PID control loop runs every 50ms, generating a log file named `balance_log.txt` with columns timestamp, tilt error, distance, motor A speed, and motor B speed. The robot reverses both motors at 50% speed for obstacle avoidance if the distance falls below 20cm. The code handles errors, initializes the GPIO pins, sets up PWM, opens the log file, and cleans up resources on all exit paths.

