```

This code initializes the GPIO pin, sets it as an output, and starts a loop that continuously reads the GPIO value. If the value is low, it debounces the signal by waiting for a certain amount of time before considering it a valid trigger. When a valid trigger occurs, it starts a video capture using raspivid and saves the file to a directory with a filename based on the current timestamp. It also appends a line to a log file containing the ISO 8601 timestamp of the motion event. The program handles errors and cleans up resources when it exits.

