This code implements PID speed control for two L298N-driven DC motors equipped with quadrature encoders on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. It uses the libgpiod library for GPIO access and the pthread library for multithreading. The code initializes the motor drivers, sets up the PID controller, and runs the main loop, which updates the PID, logs the data, and sleeps for a short period. The encoder monitoring threads are created to read the encoder values and update the PID. The signal handlers are set up to stop the motors and release the GPIO lines when the SIGINT or SIGTERM signal is received. The log file is closed and the GPIO devices are closed when the program exits.

