            send_uart(&uart, "EMERGENCY STOP!\n");
        }
    }

    // Cleanup
    close_uart(&uart);
    pigpio_close();
    return 0;
}
```

This code initializes the pigpio library, configures the GPIO pins, and sets up a main loop that reads the sensor values and logs them to the console. If all three sensors read 0, it sends the string "EMERGENCY STOP!\n" over the UART device. The program also handles signals, closes the UART port, terminates the pigpio library, and releases all resources before exiting.
